        "committer": {
          "name": "Timothy Day",
          "email": "timday@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-23 02:14:06.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21290 lnet: remove gnilnd",
        "message": "LU-21290 lnet: remove gnilnd\n\nThe Cray Gemini/Aries LND only builds against the out-of-tree\nkgni driver from the Cray XC software stack, so it is not built\nor tested by anyone outside of that environment.\n\nRemove lnet/klnds/gnilnd, the --enable-gni configure option, and\nthe RPM, Debian and DKMS packaging for kgnilnd.  Remove the GNI\nspecial cases from lctl, lnetctl and liblnetconfig, and the gni\nmodule handling from the test scripts.  Also remove the unused\nLNET_MD_GNILND flag and struct lnet_ioctl_config_gnilnd_tunables.\n\nKeep GNILND and GNIIPLND in the LND type list and in\nlibcfs_netstrfns[], so that gni NIDs can still be parsed and\nprinted and LNet routers still work with peers that use the LND.\nKeep LNET_PROTO_GNI_MAGIC reserved.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I7b474dbfdf0f93c05e96e0cab18169b96a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
